# Semgrep's built-in ignore list (semgrep 1.179, OSS/src/targeting/Semgrepignore.ml), minus its
# "Common test paths" block: test/, tests/, testsuite/, *_test.go.
#
# Semgrep uses its built-in list only when this file does not exist, and that list skips tests/, so
# `--exclude tests` coming off the command line was not enough: the suites stayed unscanned. They are
# scanned on purpose (see .github/workflows/security-code.yml, sast-semgrep), and a test's deliberate
# stand-in carries a `# nosemgrep: <rule> -- <reason>` at the line instead.
#
# Everything else below is the built-in list unchanged. .gitignore is still read as well.

# Administrative folder or file used by popular version control systems
.git
.svn
_darcs
# Paths to files and folders that are typically large and ignorable
build/
vendor/
dist/
*.min.js
.env/
.tox/
# Package managers
node_modules/
.npm/
.yarn/
.venv/
_opam/
_build/
_cargo/
